{"step_index":107,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:06:30Z","thinking":"Apple's Certified Refurbished products offer a warranty and support, including AppleCare+ eligibility within a specific timeframe after purchase. However, direct sales of these refurbished devices by Apple do not occur in India, requiring purchases to originate from other regions. Therefore, any such purchases in India are not covered under their official refurbished program.\n\n\nExamining AppleCare+ eligibility, the key factor is the original purchase date, not the secondhand purchase date; AppleCare+ must be bought within 60 days of the original sale. Warranty and AppleCare+ are global, so coverage is valid in India at Apple stores and authorized service providers. Pre-existing upfront plans can transfer with the device if the original proof of purchase is available, but monthly/annual plans are account-bound and non-transferable.\n\n\nAnalyzing AppleCare+ plans, different pricing exists for MacBook Pro 14-inch and 16-inch models, both upfront and monthly subscription options are provided for a 3-year term. The standard warranty covers only hardware defects for one year, while AppleCare+ extends this, and includes unlimited accidental damage coverage with fixed service fees. An important restriction is that AppleCare+ can only be purchased within 60 days of the original device sale date and must pass diagnostics.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"send_message","args":{"Message":"# Comprehensive Research Report: AppleCare+ for Refurbished and Second-Hand MacBook Pros in India\n\n## Executive Summary\nIn India, **you can only buy AppleCare+ for a second-hand or refurbished MacBook Pro if the machine is still within 60 days of its original retail sale date** (from Apple or an Apple Authorised Reseller). Buying from a third-party sel